{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCpVGa1ekHUxjWU4L3e1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Short answer:** The helper is `openmrsFetch` in `@openmrs/esm-api`. It does not throw or reject on a 401. By default it navigates the user to the login page and returns a promise that never settles. Other non-2xx responses reject with an `OpenmrsFetchError`. Behavior is controlled by the `redirectAuthFailure` and `followRedirects` config, and the per-call `rejectAuthFailure` flag.\n\n**Docs:** `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/openmrsFetch.md` describes the request and response shape and cancellation. It does not describe the auth-failure or error behavior. The only mention is the changeset `openmrs-esm-core/.changeset/rare-aliens-drive.md`, which says 401/403 on the session endpoint are now handled by the framework.\n\n**Implementation, in `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.ts`:**\n\n- **Request side (lines 148–163):** For REST requests, it sets `Disable-WWW-Authenticate: true` so the backend does not send a `WWW-Authenticate` challenge. A caller can override this header.\n- **Success path (lines 183–218):** A `Location` header is followed via `navigate` only for the session endpoint or on 204, and only when `followRedirects` is true. 204 responses get `data = null`. Other 2xx bodies are parsed as JSON when possible.\n- **Auth failure (lines 219–243):** This applies when the URL is the session endpoint with status 403, or when `redirectAuthFailure.enabled` is true and the status is in `redirectAuthFailure.errors` (default `[401]`). It calls `clearHistory()` and then navigates to `redirectAuthFailure.url`, or the response `Location` header, or `defaultRedirectAuthFailureUrl`. If `rejectAuthFailure` is not true, the promise either resolves (when `resolvePromise` is set) or stays pending forever (`new Promise(() => {})`), so a caller's `.catch` never runs.\n- **Other errors (lines 245–267):** The body is read as text and parsed as JSON if possible. The function then throws `OpenmrsFetchError`, which carries `response` and `responseBody`.\n- **`OpenmrsFetchError` (lines 272–283):** Its message includes the status and URL. It merges the request and response stack traces.\n\n**Config, in `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/config-schema.ts`:** `redirectAuthFailure.enabled` defaults to true, `url` defaults to `${openmrsSpaBase}/login`, `errors` defaults to `[401]`, and `resolvePromise` defaults to false. `followRedirects` defaults to true.\n\n**Not verified:** I did not read the `FetchResponse` type in full (`esm-api/src/types/fetch.ts`), and I did not check the framework's config documentation or the other `openmrsFetch` wrappers such as `useOpenmrsSWR`.\n\n**Declarations, best first:**\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.ts\", \"startLine\": 89, \"endLine\": 270},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.ts\", \"startLine\": 272, \"endLine\": 283},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.ts\", \"startLine\": 285, \"endLine\": 293},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.ts\", \"startLine\": 309, \"endLine\": 312},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/config-schema.ts\", \"startLine\": 3, \"endLine\": 3},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/config-schema.ts\", \"startLine\": 5, \"endLine\": 40},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/config-schema.ts\", \"startLine\": 42, \"endLine\": 50},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.ts\", \"startLine\": 29, \"endLine\": 38},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.ts\", \"startLine\": 305, \"endLine\": 307},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs